extracting Indian currency figures is now being investigated for correct parsing.\n\n\nThe line item extraction is failing due to the existing regular expression splitting amounts with commas, specifically in the context of Indian currency formats. The original regex `(\\d+(?:\\.\\d{1,2})?)` incorrectly splits the amount \"2,535.00\" into \"2\" and \"535.00\" because it doesn't account for commas within the number. Correcting the regex to correctly parse Indian currency numbers requires a fix that correctly groups the digits and commas. The plan is to correctly account for the format.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"PYTHONPATH=/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it /Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/venv/bin/python3 -c \"\nimport re\n\npattern = re.compile(r'(?:₹\\s*)?(\\d{1,3}(?:,\\d{2,3})*(?:\\.\\d{2})?)')\n\nline1 = '1  Bosch All-in-One Metal Hand Tool Kit  1  2,535.00  2,535.00'\nline2 = '2  Taparia Universal Tool Kit  1  1,270.00  1,270.00'\nline3 = 'Sub Total  3,805.00'\nline4 = 'Total in words: FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY RUPEES ONLY'\n\ndef parseIndianCurrency(val):\n    if not val:\n        return 0.0\n    cleaned = re.sub(r'[₹\\s]', '', str(val)).replace(',', '')\n    try:\n        return float(cleaned)\n    except ValueError:\n        return 0.0\n\nmatches1 = [m.group(1) for m in pattern.finditer(line1) if m.group(1)]\nprint('Line 1 matches:', matches1)\nprint('Parsed:', [parseIndianCurrency(x) for x in matches1])\n\nmatches2 = [m.group(1) for m in pattern.finditer(line2) if m.group(1)]\nprint('Line 2 matches:', matches2)\nprint('Parsed:', [parseIndianCurrency(x) for x in matches2])\n\nmatches3 = [m.group(1) for m in pattern.finditer(line3) if m.group(1)]\nprint('Line 3 matches:', matches3)\nprint('Parsed:', [parseIndianCurrency(x) for x in matches3])\n\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Test currency pattern extraction"}}]}
