{"step_index":1062,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T18:33:38Z","input_tokens":2920,"cache_read_tokens":183732,"output_tokens":1271,"content":"### Critical Parser Bug Resolved: Zero Comma Truncation & Word Grand Total Matching\n\nThe text parser in [utils/invoiceTextParser.js](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/invoiceTextParser.js#L17-L85) and the backend processor in [utils/clean_items.py](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/clean_items.py#L20-L80) have been updated to prevent comma splitting and correctly match printed grand totals in words.\n\n---\n\n### Key Fixes Applied\n\n#### 1. Indian Currency Regex (No Comma Splitting)\nReplaced the old regex (`/(\\d+(?:\\.\\d{1,2})?)/g`, which was splitting `\"2,535.00\"` into `\"2\"` and `\"535.00\"`) with the Indian currency pattern:\n```javascript\nconst CURRENCY_FIGURE_REGEX = /(?:₹\\s*)?(\\d{1,3}(?:,\\d{2,3})*(?:\\.\\d{2})?)/g;\n```\nThis preserves thousands digits and captures figures like `\"2,535.00\"`, `\"1,270.00\"`, `\"3,805.00\"`, and `\"4,490.00\"` as single unbroken tokens.\n\n#### 2. Exact `parseIndianCurrency` String Cleaning Helper\nImplemented in both [utils/invoiceTextParser.js](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/invoiceTextParser.js#L20-L28) and [utils/clean_items.py](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/clean_items.py#L20-L28):\n```javascript\nexport function parseIndianCurrency(val) {\n  if (!val) return 0;\n  // Strip currency symbols and whitespace, then strip commas BEFORE converting to number\n  const cleaned = String(val).replace(/